From: Panpak
Subject: wayland: bind zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 at version 5 at most

A compositor that offers version 6 (KWin 6.8) does not send main_device, and linux_dmabuf_tranche_done
dereferences the data that main_device creates. Same change as upstream commit e2d0ac2691 (GTK 4.20),
reduced to the bind. See the report in docs/PRIVATE-BUS.md.
---
--- a/gdk/wayland/gdkdisplay-wayland.c
+++ b/gdk/wayland/gdkdisplay-wayland.c
@@ -366,8 +366,9 @@
     {
       struct zwp_linux_dmabuf_feedback_v1 *feedback;
 
+      /* Version 6 of the protocol no longer sends main_device, which the handlers below rely on. */
       display_wayland->linux_dmabuf =
-        wl_registry_bind (display_wayland->wl_registry, id, &zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_interface, version);
+        wl_registry_bind (display_wayland->wl_registry, id, &zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_interface, MIN (version, 5));
       feedback = zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_get_default_feedback (display_wayland->linux_dmabuf);
       display_wayland->dmabuf_formats_info = dmabuf_formats_info_new (GDK_DISPLAY (display_wayland),
                                                                       "default",
